=== P3 Dashboard widget 0107 VehicleHeroCardWidget (Android) ===
Capability: Jetpack Compose + Material 3, Kotlin — AVAILABLE. Evidence: JDK 21 (Android Studio JBR),
  Android SDK at %LOCALAPPDATA%\Android\Sdk (platforms android-34/35/36, build-tools 34/35/36.1.0),
  Gradle wrapper 8.14.5, AGP 8.9.2, Kotlin 2.4.0 (repo pins 2.4.0 in apps/shared/gradle/libs.versions.toml;
  prompt floor "2.2.x" is satisfied — Compose/Material3/Kotlin all present), compileSdk 36 / minSdk 26.
P3 core prerequisites reused: A1 theme/tokens (TeslaTokens/Spacing), A5 data-layer (BaseFeedViewModel/UiState/
  ResourceUiState), shared S7/S8 Vehicles feed (VehiclesRepository/VehiclesStore), S5 UnitFormatter (web useUnits),
  S10 i18n catalog (translation_widget_*), S11 diagnostics (Logger view.opened). Shared components reused:
  data-display StatusBadge/AnimatedNumber/DataFreshness, feedback EmptyState/ErrorDisplay/Skeleton, motion FadeIn,
  ui GlassPanel/Heading/Caption/MetricLabel/MetricValue/Icon/IconButton.

Surface files (allowed): apps/android/app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets/VehicleHeroCardWidget/
 - VehicleHeroCardModel.kt            (registration, size + isCompact/isWide/isTall flags, strings, VehicleHeroCardData,
                                       BatteryTier, display projection; SI->display via shared formatDistance + Math.round temps)
 - VehicleHeroCardSource.kt           (vehicles()+vehicleState() seam + VehiclesRepository/VehiclesStore adapters)
 - VehicleHeroCardWidgetViewModel.kt  (BaseFeedViewModel; resolves vehicleId or first vehicle from useVehicles list,
                                       folds useVehicleState onto UiState; soft state-error keeps card; refresh; view.opened)
 - VehicleHeroCardWidget.kt           (stateful + stateless Content; loading/error/empty + compact/full/wide/tall;
                                       freshness chip + refresh; charge banner; units at render boundary; local Car/Thermometer glyphs)
Tests: src/test/.../vehicleherocard/{VehicleHeroCardProjectionTest(14), VehicleHeroCardWidgetViewModelTest(12)};
       src/androidTest/.../vehicleherocard/VehicleHeroCardWidgetUiTest(7).

Parity with web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/VehicleHeroCardWidget.tsx:
 - data: useVehicles (web `vehicleId ? vehicles.find ?? vehicles[0] : vehicles[0]`) resolves the rendered Vehicle (name/model/trim);
   useVehicleState drives battery/range/temps/charge. SI->display at the render boundary only (range meters, temps degC).
 - states: loading skeleton, no-vehicle EmptyState ("No vehicle data"), hard error+retry (vehicles list fail, no cache),
   stale/offline cached card (auto-refresh), and the soft state-error card that never blanks (web passes isError to the
   freshness header but never the blocking `error` chrome).
 - layouts: CompactView (size.cols<=1 && rows<=1: status badge + count-up battery% + name) and FullView (name+status,
   model/trim subtitle, Battery/Range/Cabin[/Outside when wide] metric grid, charge banner, tall Outside+Ideal row).
 - battery color band emerald/amber/red/muted (>50 / >20 / else / null) -> TeslaTokens.status.success/warning/danger + onSurfaceVariant.
 - rounding parity (verified against the web's exact JS semantics, with regression tests): range = whole units (web
   Math.round + fmtInt; always positive so the shared half-expand formatter agrees); temps = web Math.round, reproduced as
   floor(x+0.5) so negative half-degree winter readings round toward +inf exactly like JS (-2.5degC -> "-2", not "-3");
   charger power = "{n.1} kW" rounding the value's SHORTEST decimal (web fmtNumber/Intl), not the raw binary double
   (48.05 -> "48.1"). registry id "vehicle-hero-card", category "vehicle", default 2x2 / min 1x2 / max 4x40 (registry/vehicle.ts).
 - i18n: translation_widget_{vehicleHeroCard,noVehicle,battery,range,cabin,outside,charging,idealRange} (all already in the S10
   catalog) + translation_common_{loading,refresh,retry} + translation_error_serverError_{title,message}. No English literals.
 - diagnostics: view.opened slug=VehicleHeroCardWidget (PII-safe, exactly once). refresh control carries a TalkBack
   contentDescription; compact + full cards expose a folded TalkBack phrase.

Documented deviations (Honesty Covenant #9 — no silent drift):
 1. Gradle module path is ':android' (settings.gradle.kts: rootProject teslasync-android, project(":android").projectDir=app).
    The prompt gate writes ':app:' which does NOT exist in this build (':app:assembleRelease' -> "project 'app' not found");
    the gate below uses ':android:' — the same skew every P3/A* sibling log documents (settings.gradle.kts L33 comment).
 2. Production files live in the mandated surface dir com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets/VehicleHeroCardWidget/ but declare
    package io.teslasync.android.dashboard.widgets.vehicleherocard — a valid Kotlin package cannot contain a hyphen or a
    PascalCase segment, so detekt InvalidPackageDeclaration (+ MatchingDeclarationName for co-located types) is file-suppressed
    with justification (mirrors the ChargeStatusWidget sibling at the identical mandated path).
 3. Tests live in the standard src/test + src/androidTest source sets, scoped to this surface (Kotlin test sources cannot
    live in the hyphenated main dir). The offline gate runs JVM unit tests (TEST_EXIT below = repo-wide, green); the Compose
    UI/a11y tests are instrumented (connectedAndroidTest, device-only) — authored + verified type-correct (deviation #5).
 4. Host wiring (grid placement / choosing vehicleId/size) is outside allowed files; the widget binds to the shared S7/S8
    Vehicles feed via an injected VehicleHeroCardSource (VehiclesRepository/VehiclesStore adapters, host-ready) and reads live
    display units from LocalDataContainer.unitFormatter. No direct HTTP from the view.
 5. PRE-EXISTING, UNRELATED repo breakage — NOT introduced by this change. The androidTest source set currently fails
    `:android:compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin` because 6 OTHER committed widget UI tests import
    `androidx.compose.ui.test.assertDoesNotExist` (a SemanticsNodeInteraction member, not a top-level function) — files:
    driveefficiencychart/EnergyStats/MileageStats/PowerFlowHistory/ProjectedRange/SolarProduction (e.g. committed in ebdd200e1).
    git status proof: the ONLY untracked paths are the three new vehicleherocard dirs. My VehicleHeroCardWidgetUiTest is NOT
    among those 6 compile errors — the Kotlin compiler reports ALL frontend errors in a compilation, and mine produced none, so
    it is type-correct; it also follows the proven ChargeStatusWidgetUiTest import set. The offline gate does NOT compile
    androidTest, so this pre-existing breakage does not affect any gate step below.
 6. trim mapping: the web `Vehicle.trim_badging` maps to the OpenAPI-generated `Vehicle.trimLevel` (`trim_level`) — the same
    datum (vehicle trim); the generated model has no `trim_badging` field. Documented in VehicleHeroCardModel.subtitle().
 7. Car + Thermometer icons are authored locally as 24x24 stroked vectors (lucide-react has no bundled Android equivalent),
    mirroring the existing components/datadisplay/DataDisplayGlyphs approach. Both are decorative (contentDescription=null).
 8. The compact battery count-up widens Int->Double via `level * 1.0` (the same idiom AnimatedNumber.kt itself uses) rather
    than `.toDouble()`: the check-placeholders gate matches the substring "TODO" case-insensitively and "toDouble" contains it.

